2022.description:
The proposed project aims at establishing a port between GHC and [MMTk](https://www.mmtk.io/) -- an external memory management toolkit that provides languages with a set of memory management primitives and garbage collectors. 

The current existing GHC storage manager (GHCSM) has a sophisticated generational GC; However, it's also optimized and integrated into GHC's runtime, making it difficult to switch to a broader range of collectors. It would be beneficial to generalize GHC's runtime, make it separable from GHCSM, and connect it with a suite of different garbage collections from MMTk.


To achieve this goal, we propose to:
1. Refactor GHC's runtime system to more effectively abstract over storage management operations;
2. Introduce a storage management backend using MMTk's trivial no-GC collection plan;
3. Integrate write barriers necessary for generational collection with MMTk;
4. Introduce support for MMTk's semi-space and mark-sweep GC plans.
